{
  "_meta": {
    "scenario": "kerbin-plane-change-node",
    "notes": "The kerbin-lko-equator parking orbit with one burn planned on it: 1,098 m/s of pure normal at UT 1235167, ten minutes ahead, taking the plane from 0 to 28 degrees. The node's own post-burn patch chain is what MapView samples the CYAN track from, and the amber current-orbit track runs under it along the equator, so the two say what the burn changes. No fixture carried a `vessel.maneuver` node before this one, so `maneuverSegments` returned an empty array in every render and the cyan half of the overlay had never been drawn. The post-burn ascending node is where the craft is at the burn (113.96 degrees of the 1895 s period after epoch), which is why the crossing sits under the node rather than at longitude zero. Its first render found a bug: the polyline was split at the PROPAGATED date line while the canvas draws through Kerbin's 90-degree texture offset, so the pair of samples straddling the drawn seam was stroked as one line clean across the map. Every fixture before this one was equatorial, and a spurious full-width line along latitude zero sits exactly on top of the track that drew it. See `groundTrackWrap.ts`."
  },
